Model expected business failures explicitly. Hide recoverable details only where callers do not need them to preserve correctness.

> These different kinds of errors require different implementations.

Source: [Q15](/lore/durability-bibliography#q15); [B7](/lore/durability-bibliography#b7-domain-modeling-made-functional), [B10](/lore/durability-bibliography#b10-a-philosophy-of-software-design).

## Failure it prevents

A broken execution becomes a permanent business refusal, or a permanent refusal triggers endless retry.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

`Schema.TaggedError` and `Effect.catchTag` carry named expected outcomes. Classification and [defect](/lore/effect-basics) policy remain domain decisions. A [service](/lore/services-capture-dependencies) seam can own recoverable mechanics.

Source: `packages/effect/src/Schema.ts`, `packages/effect/src/Effect.ts`, `packages/effect/src/Context.ts`, `packages/effect/src/Layer.ts`.

## How to check

Exercise each declared failure category. Verify retry, refusal, escalation, and uncertain outcomes remain distinguishable. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Cleanup can be an idempotent postcondition](/lore/cleanup-can-be-an-idempotent-postcondition), [Pure cores reduce timeline coupling](/lore/pure-cores-reduce-timelines).

Connect this to [the existing rat-stack guidance](/lore/error-model).

